hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16068","Affan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zurarah al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather al-Harith ibn Amr, that he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I said, may my father be for you, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. He said: May Allah forgive you. He said, and he was upon his she-camel al-Adba. He said, so I turned to him from the other side, hoping he would single me out apart from the people, and I said, seek forgiveness for me. He said: May Allah forgive you. A man said, O Messenger of Allah, the fara and the atirah. He said: Whoever wishes consecrates a fara, and whoever wishes does not, and whoever wishes slaughters an atirah, and whoever wishes does not, in sheep is a sacrifice. Then he said: Verily your blood and your wealth are forbidden upon you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours. And Affan said once, Yahya ibn Zurarah al-Sahmi narrated to me, he said, my father narrated to me, from his grandfather al-Harith."
